 true] [17592186320858 1111 #uuid "8fecbee0-2afd-58ac-9fad-158504fd7cef" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1017 #edb/ref 17592186320860 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1089 "q-280528" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1100 "A falcon flies from the origin with a constant velocity of $(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the falcon to the origin after $1$ hour.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1113 #uuid "d4b26847-5f09-546b-bd05-0cd5caf581b4" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320859 1145 "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-6i+8j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the falcon after $t=1\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-6i+8j)(1) \\\\  & =(-6i+8j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the falcon to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|-6i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320861 13194139534934 true] [17592186320860 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534934 true] [17592186320860 1041 "field-1" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320860 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320861 13194139534934 true] [17592186320860 1110 #uuid "7633c9f3-0ab1-52bd-b43a-944dfa15e249" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320861 1034 "10" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320861 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534934 true] [17592186320861 1111 #uuid "f990279b-d4f2-5303-900c-8ee6d93432df" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1017 #edb/ref 17592186320863 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1089 "q-280537" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1100 "A helicopter starts from the position $(5i+2j)\\,\\text{m}$ with an initial velocity of $(-i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ and an acceleration of $(i-j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Find the distance from the helicopter to the origin $(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1113 #uuid "898c8dfc-9e20-53d9-8140-6db68ccf63e0" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320862 1145 "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=5i+2j,\\,u=-i+3j,\\,a=i-j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the helicopter after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(5i+2j)+(-i+3j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(i-j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+2(i-j) \\\\  & =(5i+2j)+(-2i+6j)+(2i-2j) \\\\  & =(5i+6j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the helicopter to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|5i+6j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{61}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320864 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320865 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1041 "field-1" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320865 13194139534934 true] [17592186320863 1110 #uuid "062476d8-3544-5a77-97c8-52a9ab626fd6" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320864 1034 "11" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320864 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534934 true] [17592186320864 1111 #uuid "17e57a88-9de7-581a-bfa2-fe8565c21cc4" 13194139534934 true] [17592186320865 1034 "\\sqrt{61}" 1319413